## graphify (vendored in full)

- Location in this repo: `.claude/skills/graphify/` (version 0.9.16)
- Upstream: https://github.com/Graphify-Labs/graphify
- Author: Safi Shamsi
- License: MIT (SPDX: MIT)
- Local modifications (not in upstream):
  - `SKILL.md` Step 1, and the extras tips in `SKILL.md` and
    `references/add-watch.md`, install `graphifyy` only at the version in
    `.claude/skills/graphify/.graphify_version`, with no `--upgrade` and no
    `--break-system-packages` fallback. Setup stops and asks the owner when the
    pin is missing or the pinned install fails (skill-safety-59f9427a).
  - Semantic extraction dispatches read-only subagents that return their JSON
    as text for the parent to write, instead of general-purpose subagents
    holding Write and Bash, and `/graphify add` asks the owner to confirm each
    URL before fetching it (skill-safety-5f9c118a). Ceiling: where the
    harness's read-only subagent type still carries a shell, the instruction
    not to run shell commands is prompt-level only.
  - `SKILL.md` semantic extraction uses Gemini only when `GEMINI_API_KEY` is set
    and the owner confirms uploading this corpus; `GOOGLE_API_KEY` no longer
    selects it, and without a yes the subagent path runs
    (skill-safety-39614de9). Ceiling: this governs what the skill tells the
    agent to run, not what the graphify CLI does on its own. `graphify
    extract` and `graphify cluster-only`/`label` auto-select a backend from
    any provider key in the environment (Gemini, Google, Moonshot, Anthropic,
    OpenAI, DeepSeek, Azure), from `AWS_PROFILE`/`AWS_REGION`/
    `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` alone (bedrock) or from `OLLAMA_BASE_URL`, so a CLI
    call made outside the flows below, by hand or by an agent ignoring them,
    uploads corpus text without a prompt.
  - The CLI flows the skill mandates pass graphify's no-LLM option:
    `references/update.md` runs `graphify cluster-only . --no-label`,
    `references/github-and-merge.md` runs `graphify extract <dir> --code-only`
    and no longer tells the agent to add `--backend` for whichever API key is
    set, and `references/extraction-spec.md`'s rebuild hint adds
    `--code-only`. A `--backend` flag, and `graphify label`, are used only
    after the owner confirms the upload to that provider. `SKILL.md` no longer
    claims graphify reads no other provider key (skill-safety-13ef11d9).
  - `references/query.md`'s three `save-result` steps (query, path, explain)
    pass the answer through a quoted heredoc into a temporary file read with
    `--answer-file`, and single-quote the question, node labels and any
    `--correction`, instead of substituting the answer into a double-quoted
    shell argument where backticks and `$(...)` execute (skill-safety-eabeab65).
  - `SKILL.md`'s fast path and query stub, and `references/query.md`'s
    `graphify query`, `graphify path` and `graphify explain` calls,
    single-quote the question and node labels with `'\''` escaping instead of
    double-quoting them; the inline fallbacks pass those values as
    single-quoted arguments read from `sys.argv` instead of pasting them into
    the double-quoted `-c` program. `SKILL.md` Step 5 writes the community
    labels to a temporary file through a quoted heredoc and reads them with
    `json.load`, instead of substituting a model-written dict into the
    program. `references/query.md`'s quoting rule names all of these
    (skill-safety-92d2d3a1). Ceiling: the `/graphify` usage lines at the top
    of `SKILL.md` are invocations a user types, not shell, and keep upstream's
    double quotes.
  - `references/transcribe.md` exports `GRAPHIFY_WHISPER_PROMPT`, a domain
    hint built from god-node labels, in single quotes with `'\''` escaping
    instead of double quotes, and `references/query.md`'s quoting rule names
    it (skill-safety-7a4afcd8).
- Generated content: the `## graphify` section formerly in CLAUDE.md was
  generated by `graphify claude install` (graphify 0.9.16); its four rules now
  live, locally modified only by relocation, in `.claude/rules/graphify.md`.

